## Specific Governance Changes

### Change Type
- [x] Mechanism Innovation
- [x] Other: Account Abstraction Infrastructure Standardization

### Detailed Change Content

#### Smart Wallet Standard

**New Clause**:
> The OKX ecosystem shall adopt OKX Smart Wallet as the canonical non-custodial smart wallet standard.
>
> All wallet deployments and integrations must follow a unified execution, authorization, and upgrade governance framework supporting:
>
> 1. EIP-4337 account abstraction execution
> 2. EIP-7702 delegated execution compatibility
> 3. Relayer-based gasless transaction execution
> 4. Replay-protected cross-chain authorization
> 5. Modular validator-based authentication
> 6. Governance-scoped and auditable upgradeability
>
> All wallet contracts must remain independently audited, privilege-free, and non-custodial post-deployment.

**Explanation**:
This proposal establishes a unified wallet infrastructure layer for the OKX ecosystem.

The proposed architecture reduces integration fragmentation, standardizes wallet security assumptions, simplifies cross-chain execution, and improves onboarding usability through account abstraction capabilities.

The wallet framework additionally introduces replay-resistant cross-chain execution, Passkey/WebAuthn authentication, relayer-based gas abstraction, and modular validator systems while preserving full user asset custody.

